<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/20th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Attack on Pearl Harbor</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1941">1941</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Pearl Harbor · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-world-war">Second World War</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The attack on Pearl Harbor was the surprise attack by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/empire-of-japan">Empire of Japan</a>'s naval air forces on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a> Pacific Fleet in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hawaii">Hawaii</a> on 7 December 1941. It aimed to cripple American naval power so <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a> could seize resources in South-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/east-asia">East Asia</a>. It brought the United States into the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-world-war">Second World War</a>, a decision that led to Japan's eventual defeat.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/attack-on-pearl-harbor.jpg" alt="Attack on Pearl Harbor" width="320" height="227" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Imperial Japanese Navy · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Attack_on_Pearl_Harbor_Japanese_planes_view.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
